{"author":{"id":"86dc3c885e4fa466d19699d4a5e74c240f1c9d6b23f4e62ea2d2d8e359bd1711"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789629540,"nonce":"VNAaj+l+1AdFZqqGrob2HmCE2ds=","message":"Authoritative acceptance criteria:\n\nScope: v0.9.1 follow-up.\n\n`print` accepts zero or more expressions. It evaluates those expressions in source order and produces one output entry by concatenating their display values with no implicit separator. This permits mixed string and numeric output without adding string concatenation or template strings.\n\nExample: `print(\"x: \", x);` produces `x: ` followed by the value of `x` in the same output entry.\n\nThis issue records the request only; it does not authorize implementation.","files":null}]}